{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell00",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Cosmo-statistics with type Ia Supernovae\n",
    "#### Authors: Benjamín Carrillo, Nicolás Miranda<br>Universidad Técnica Federico Santa María\n",
    "\n",
    "##### In this notebook, we developed a code to estimate the $H_0$ and $q_0$ parameters for ΛCDM cosmological model, using data from the Pantheon+ catalogue and SHOES collaboration (Brout et al. 2022) for the type Ia supernovae magnitude and redshift. We guide the user across this notebook and the calculations presented in the corresponding paper Constraints from Type Ia supernovae: Cosmography or $\Lambda\text{CDM}$: constraints from Type Ia supernovae"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell01",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Cell 1: Dependences\\\n",
    "We first need the python packages below:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "cell02",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np # For the matemathical operations\n",
    "import pandas as pd # For the data manipulation\n",
    "from scipy.optimize import minimize_scalar # For the minimization of the function\n",
    "from scipy.optimize import brentq # For the uncertainty intervals\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt # For the plotting of the results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell03",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Cell 2: Data extraction\\\n",
    "Using the file \"Pantheon+SHOES.dat\" from th github of the collaboration https://github.com/PantheonPlusSH0ES/DataRelease.\n",
    "We need the columns for the redshift corrected for peculiar velocities and the movement of the Earth relative to the Hubble frame, the apparent magnitude corrected by ISM extinction, and its corresponding error. Additionally, we used the distance modulus $(\\mu)$ measured by the SHOES collaboration, this $\\mu$ used Cepheids at the same redshift to calibrate the absolute magnitude $M$ "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "cell04",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data = \"Pantheon+SH0ES.dat\"\n",
    "dt = pd.read_csv(data, sep=r\"\\s+\")\n",
    "\n",
    "dt_b = dt.query(\"IS_CALIBRATOR == 0 and 0.023 < zHD < 0.15\")  # Low z, no calibrators\n",
    "dt_h = dt.query(\"IS_CALIBRATOR == 0 and zHD > 0.01\")  # Hubble flow, no calibrators\n",
    "\n",
    "# Low-z sample (q0, H0)\n",
    "z_b = dt_b[\"zHD\"].values\n",
    "m_b = dt_b[\"m_b_corr\"].values\n",
    "sigma_b = dt_b[\"m_b_corr_err_DIAG\"].values\n",
    "mu_b = dt_b[\"MU_SH0ES\"].values\n",
    "sigma_mu_b = dt_b[\"MU_SH0ES_ERR_DIAG\"].values\n",
    "\n",
    "# High-z sample (Om)\n",
    "z_h = dt_h[\"zHD\"].values\n",
    "m_h = dt_h[\"m_b_corr\"].values\n",
    "sigma_h = dt_h[\"m_b_corr_err_DIAG\"].values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell05",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Cell 3: Marginalized $\\chi^2$ for the cosmographic model\\\n",
    "At low redshift, the luminosity distance can be expanded in terms of the deceleration parameter $q_0$:\n",
    "$$d_L^C(z; H_0, q_0) = \\frac{c}{H_0}\\left[z + \\frac{1-q_0}{2}z^2\\right]$$\n",
    "Since $H_0$ and the absolute magnitude $M$ are degenerate, we define $G_i = m_i - 5\\log_{10}\\left(F(z_i; q_0)/10\\right)$, where $F$ is the luminosity distance without the factor $c/H_0$, and marginalize over $\\mathcal{M} = M - 5\\log_{10}H_0 + 25$. The function returns the marginalized $\\chi^2$, which depends only on $q_0$:\n",
    "$$\\chi^2(q_0) = \\chi_0^2 - \\frac{A^2}{B}, \\qquad \\chi_0^2 = \\sum_i \\frac{G_i^2}{\\sigma_i^2}, \\quad A = \\sum_i \\frac{G_i}{\\sigma_i^2}, \\quad B = \\sum_i \\frac{1}{\\sigma_i^2}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "cell06",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "c = 299792.458 # speed of light in km/s\n",
    "\n",
    "def marg_q(q, z, m, sigma):\n",
    "\n",
    "    F = z + ((1-q)*z**2)/2  # Cosmography relation for luminosity distance\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Marginalization parameters:\n",
    "    \n",
    "    G = m - 5 * np.log10(F/10)\n",
    "    X_0 = np.sum((G**2)/sigma**2)\n",
    "    A = np.sum(G/sigma**2)\n",
    "    B = np.sum(1/sigma**2)\n",
    "    Xi2 = X_0 - (A**2)/(B)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return Xi2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell07",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Cell 4: Marginalized $\\chi^2$ for the ΛCDM model\\\n",
    "For a flat universe with matter and cosmological constant, the luminosity distance is:\n",
    "$$d_L^{\\Lambda CDM}(z; H_0, \\Omega_{M}) = c\\,\\frac{1+z}{H_0}\\int_0^z \\frac{dz'}{E(z')}, \\qquad E(z) = \\sqrt{\\Omega_{M}(1+z)^3 + (1-\\Omega_{M})}$$\n",
    "The integral is computed numerically with the trapezoidal rule for each $z_i$. We use the same marginalization over $\\mathcal{M}$ as in Cell 3, so the $\\chi^2$ depends only on $\\Omega_M$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "cell08",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def marg_Om(Om, z, m, sigma):\n",
    "\n",
    "    z_values = np.linspace(0, z, 1000)  # Integration grid for each z_i\n",
    "    integrand = 1 / np.sqrt(Om * (1 + z_values)**3 + (1 - Om))  # 1/E(z)\n",
    "    integral = np.trapezoid(integrand, z_values, axis=0)  # Integral for each z_i\n",
    "\n",
    "    F = (1 + z) * integral  # ΛCDM relation for luminosity distance\n",
    "\n",
    "    G = m - 5 * np.log10(F/10)\n",
    "    X_0 = np.sum((G**2)/sigma**2)\n",
    "    A = np.sum(G/sigma**2)\n",
    "    B = np.sum(1/sigma**2)\n",
    "    Xi2 = X_0 - (A**2)/(B)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return Xi2\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell09",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Cell 5: $\\chi^2$ with the SH0ES distance modulus\\\n",
    "To obtain $H_0$, we use the distance modulus $\\mu_i = m_i - M$ from the SH0ES collaboration, where $M$ was calibrated with Cepheids. Since $M$ is known, the degeneracy with $H_0$ is broken and we can fit $H_0$ directly, with $q_0$ fixed:\n",
    "$$\\chi^2(H_0) = \\sum_i \\left(\\frac{\\mu_i - \\mu^{\\rm teo}(z_i; H_0, q_0)}{\\sigma_{\\mu,i}}\\right)^2, \\qquad \\mu^{\\rm teo} = 5\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac{d_L}{\\rm Mpc}\\right) + 25$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "cell10",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def X2(H0, z, mu, sigma_mu, q):\n",
    "\n",
    "    F = z + ((1-q)*z**2)/2  # Cosmography relation for luminosity distance\n",
    "    dL = c * F / H0  # Luminosity distance [Mpc]\n",
    "    mu_teo = 5 * np.log10(dL) + 25  # Theoretical distance modulus\n",
    "\n",
    "    Xi2 = np.sum(((mu - mu_teo)**2)/sigma_mu**2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return Xi2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell11",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Cell 6: Minimization\\\n",
    "We minimize each $\\chi^2$ with `minimize_scalar`:\n",
    "- $q_0$ and $H_0$ are obtained from the low redshift sample ($0.023 < z < 0.15$), where the cosmographic expansion is valid and the peculiar velocities are small (same range used by SH0ES).\n",
    "- $\\Omega_M$ is obtained from the whole Hubble flow ($z > 0.01$), since the ΛCDM distance is valid at any redshift.\n",
    "- From $\\Omega_M$ we also compute the deceleration parameter predicted by flat ΛCDM, $q_0 = \\frac{3}{2}\\Omega_M - 1$, and $H_0$ is obtained for both values of $q_0$.\n",
    "\n",
    "The calibrator supernovae (Cepheid hosts) are excluded in all the fits."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "cell12",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "q0: -0.5184028810121344\n",
      "Om: 0.34907746520227034\n",
      "q0_calc: -0.4763838021965945\n",
      "H0_q0: 73.19565645287241\n",
      "H0_q0_calc: 73.11014686344683\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "q0 = minimize_scalar(marg_q, bounds=(-3, 2), args=(z_b, m_b, sigma_b), method=\"bounded\")\n",
    "q0 = q0.x\n",
    "Om = minimize_scalar(marg_Om, bounds=(0, 1), args=(z_h, m_h, sigma_h), method=\"bounded\")\n",
    "Om = Om.x\n",
    "q0_calc = 1.5*Om - 1\n",
    "\n",
    "H0_q0 = minimize_scalar(X2, bounds=(50, 100), args=(z_b, mu_b, sigma_mu_b, q0), method=\"bounded\")\n",
    "H0_q0_calc = minimize_scalar(X2, bounds=(50, 100), args=(z_b, mu_b, sigma_mu_b, q0_calc), method=\"bounded\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"q0:\", q0)\n",
    "print(\"Om:\", Om)\n",
    "print(\"q0_calc:\", q0_calc)\n",
    "print(\"H0_q0:\", H0_q0.x)\n",
    "print(\"H0_q0_calc:\", H0_q0_calc.x)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell13",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Cell 7: Uncertainties\\\n",
    "For a single parameter, the $1\\sigma$ interval ($\\approx 68.3\\%$) is given by the values where the $\\chi^2$ increases by one unit with respect to its minimum, $\\chi^2(x) = \\chi^2_{\\min} + 1$. We find both limits with `brentq`, assuming independent gaussian errors (diagonal errors of the catalogue).\n",
    "- The uncertainty of $q_0$ derived from ΛCDM is propagated from $\\Omega_M$ through the linear relation $q_0 = \\frac{3}{2}\\Omega_M - 1$.\n",
    "- The uncertainties of $H_0$ are conditional to a fixed $q_0$, so they do not include the uncertainty of $q_0$ nor the systematic covariances between supernovae."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "cell14",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "UNCERTAINTIES (Δχ² = 1):\n",
      "q0 cosmographic = -0.5184 (+0.2307/-0.2347)\n",
      "Om (ΛCDM) = 0.3491 (+0.0190/-0.0186)\n",
      "q0 from ΛCDM = -0.4764 (+0.0285/-0.0279)\n",
      "H0 [q0 cosmographic fixed] = 73.1957 (+0.2941/-0.2929) km/s/Mpc\n",
      "H0 [q0 from ΛCDM fixed] = 73.1101 (+0.2937/-0.2926) km/s/Mpc\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def intervalo_1sigma(func, mejor, limites):\n",
    "\n",
    "    chi2_min = func(mejor)  # χ² at the best fit\n",
    "\n",
    "    def delta(x):\n",
    "        return func(x) - chi2_min - 1.0  # Δχ² - 1\n",
    "\n",
    "    inferior, superior = limites\n",
    "    if delta(inferior) <= 0 or delta(superior) <= 0:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"The 1σ interval is not contained in the chosen bounds\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    x_inferior = brentq(delta, inferior, mejor)  # Lower 1σ limit\n",
    "    x_superior = brentq(delta, mejor, superior)  # Upper 1σ limit\n",
    "\n",
    "    return mejor - x_inferior, x_superior - mejor\n",
    "\n",
    "# q0 from cosmography (low z, uncalibrated magnitudes)\n",
    "err_q0_menos, err_q0_mas = intervalo_1sigma(\n",
    "    lambda q: marg_q(q, z_b, m_b, sigma_b), q0, (-3, 2)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Om from ΛCDM (Hubble flow)\n",
    "err_Om_menos, err_Om_mas = intervalo_1sigma(\n",
    "    lambda om: marg_Om(om, z_h, m_h, sigma_h), Om, (0, 1)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# q0 from ΛCDM (linear propagation)\n",
    "err_q0_calc_menos = 1.5 * err_Om_menos\n",
    "err_q0_calc_mas = 1.5 * err_Om_mas\n",
    "\n",
    "# H0 with fixed q0 (conditional errors)\n",
    "err_H0_q0_menos, err_H0_q0_mas = intervalo_1sigma(\n",
    "    lambda H: X2(H, z_b, mu_b, sigma_mu_b, q0), H0_q0.x, (50, 100)\n",
    ")\n",
    "err_H0_calc_menos, err_H0_calc_mas = intervalo_1sigma(\n",
    "    lambda H: X2(H, z_b, mu_b, sigma_mu_b, q0_calc),\n",
    "    H0_q0_calc.x, (50, 100)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"UNCERTAINTIES (Δχ² = 1):\")\n",
    "print(f\"q0 cosmographic = {q0:.4f} (+{err_q0_mas:.4f}/-{err_q0_menos:.4f})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Om (ΛCDM) = {Om:.4f} (+{err_Om_mas:.4f}/-{err_Om_menos:.4f})\")\n",
    "print(f\"q0 from ΛCDM = {q0_calc:.4f} (+{err_q0_calc_mas:.4f}/-{err_q0_calc_menos:.4f})\")\n",
    "print(f\"H0 [q0 cosmographic fixed] = {H0_q0.x:.4f} (+{err_H0_q0_mas:.4f}/-{err_H0_q0_menos:.4f}) km/s/Mpc\")\n",
    "print(f\"H0 [q0 from ΛCDM fixed] = {H0_q0_calc.x:.4f} (+{err_H0_calc_mas:.4f}/-{err_H0_calc_menos:.4f}) km/s/Mpc\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell15",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Cell 8: Sensitivity of $H_0$ to $q_0$\\\n",
    "Since $H_0$ was obtained with a fixed $q_0$, we check how much it changes when $q_0$ moves within its $1\\sigma$ interval. This is only a diagnostic: these shifts are not added to the uncertainties of Cell 7, because both estimations use related supernovae and are correlated."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "cell16",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "SENSITIVITY (not a total interval for H0):\n",
      "Varying q0 within its 1σ interval, H0 moves between 72.726 and 73.673 km/s/Mpc\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def mejor_H0_para_q(q):\n",
    "\n",
    "    return minimize_scalar(\n",
    "        X2, bounds=(50, 100), args=(z_b, mu_b, sigma_mu_b, q), method=\"bounded\"\n",
    "    ).x  # Best H0 for a given q0\n",
    "\n",
    "H0_extremo_q_inferior = mejor_H0_para_q(q0 - err_q0_menos)  # H0 at the lower limit of q0\n",
    "H0_extremo_q_superior = mejor_H0_para_q(q0 + err_q0_mas)  # H0 at the upper limit of q0\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"SENSITIVITY (not a total interval for H0):\")\n",
    "print(f\"Varying q0 within its 1σ interval, H0 moves between {min(H0_extremo_q_inferior, H0_extremo_q_superior):.3f} and {max(H0_extremo_q_inferior, H0_extremo_q_superior):.3f} km/s/Mpc\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell17",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Cell 9: Luminosity distances\\\n",
    "With the fitted parameters ($H_0$, $q_0$, $\\Omega_M$), we define the luminosity distances of both models in Mpc, to compare them with the data in the plots."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "cell18",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def dL_cosmo(z, H0, q):\n",
    "\n",
    "    F = z + ((1-q)*z**2)/2  # Cosmogrpahy expansion\n",
    "    dL = c * F / H0  # Luminosity distance [Mpc]\n",
    "\n",
    "    return dL\n",
    "\n",
    "def dL_LCDM(z, H0, Om):\n",
    "\n",
    "    z_values = np.linspace(0, z, 1000)  # Integration grid for each z_i\n",
    "    integrand = 1 / np.sqrt(Om * (1 + z_values)**3 + (1 - Om))  # 1/E(z)\n",
    "    integral = np.trapezoid(integrand, z_values, axis=0)  # Integral for each z_i\n",
    "\n",
    "    dL = c * (1 + z) * integral / H0  # Luminosity distance [Mpc]\n",
    "\n",
    "    return dL"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell19",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Cell 10: Hubble diagram\\\n",
    "We plot the distance modulus of the Hubble flow supernovae from SH0ES, together with the ΛCDM and cosmographic models evaluated with the fitted parameters. The lower panel shows the residuals with respect to ΛCDM. The dotted line marks $z = 0.15$, the upper limit of the cosmographic fit: beyond this value the cosmographic curve is an extrapolation, and it departs from the data as the expansion is no longer valid."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "cell20",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x700 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Data for the plot (Hubble flow)\n",
    "z_h = dt_h[\"zHD\"].values\n",
    "mu_h = dt_h[\"MU_SH0ES\"].values\n",
    "sigma_mu_h = dt_h[\"MU_SH0ES_ERR_DIAG\"].values\n",
    "\n",
    "# Theoretical curves\n",
    "z_graf = np.logspace(np.log10(0.01), np.log10(2.3), 500)  # Redshift grid\n",
    "mu_c = 5 * np.log10(dL_cosmo(z_graf, H0_q0.x, q0)) + 25  # Cosmopgraphic model\n",
    "mu_l = 5 * np.log10(dL_LCDM(z_graf, H0_q0_calc.x, Om)) + 25  # ΛCDM model\n",
    "\n",
    "# Residuals for ΛCDM\n",
    "mu_teo_h = 5 * np.log10(dL_LCDM(z_h, H0_q0_calc.x, Om)) + 25  # ΛCDM in the real z values\n",
    "res_h = mu_h - mu_teo_h  # Residuals\n",
    "res_c = mu_c - mu_l  # cosmographic - ΛCDM\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(2, 1, figsize=(8, 7), sharex=True, gridspec_kw={\"height_ratios\": [3, 1]})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Hubble diagram\n",
    "ax1.errorbar(z_h, mu_h, yerr=sigma_mu_h, fmt=\"o\", ms=2, color=\"gray\", alpha=0.4, label=\"Pantheon+SH0ES\")\n",
    "ax1.plot(z_graf, mu_l, color=\"C0\", label=rf\"ΛCDM ($\\Omega_M$ = {Om:.3f})\")\n",
    "ax1.plot(z_graf, mu_c, color=\"C3\", ls=\"--\", label=rf\"Cosmographic ($q_0$ = {q0:.3f})\")\n",
    "ax1.axvline(0.15, color=\"k\", ls=\":\", lw=1, label=r\"Cosmographic limit ($z$ = 0.15)\")  # Cosmographic limit for the fit\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel(r\"$\\mu$\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax1.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Residuals plot\n",
    "ax2.errorbar(z_h, res_h, yerr=sigma_mu_h, fmt=\"o\", ms=2, color=\"gray\", alpha=0.4)\n",
    "ax2.plot(z_graf, res_c, color=\"C3\", ls=\"--\")\n",
    "ax2.axhline(0, color=\"C0\")\n",
    "ax2.axvline(0.15, color=\"k\", ls=\":\", lw=1)\n",
    "ax2.set_xscale(\"log\")\n",
    "ax2.set_xlabel(r\"$z$\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel(r\"$\\mu - \\mu_{\\Lambda CDM}$\",fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax2.set_ylim(-1, 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(\"Hubble_diagram.png\", dpi=300)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell21",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Cell 11: $\\chi^2$ profiles\\\n",
    "We plot $\\Delta\\chi^2 = \\chi^2 - \\chi^2_{\\min}$ as a function of $q_0$ and $\\Omega_M$. The dashed line marks $\\Delta\\chi^2 = 1$ and the shaded region corresponds to the $1\\sigma$ interval obtained in Cell 7."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "cell22",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1100x450 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Parameter ranges around the best-fit values\n",
    "q_values = np.linspace(q0 - 3*err_q0_menos,\n",
    "                       q0 + 3*err_q0_mas, 300)\n",
    "\n",
    "Om_values = np.linspace(Om - 3*err_Om_menos,\n",
    "                        Om + 3*err_Om_mas, 300)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Evaluate marginalized chi-square functions\n",
    "chi2_q = np.array([\n",
    "    marg_q(q, z_b, m_b, sigma_b) for q in q_values\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "chi2_Om = np.array([\n",
    "    marg_Om(om, z_h, m_h, sigma_h) for om in Om_values\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Delta chi-square\n",
    "delta_q = chi2_q - marg_q(q0, z_b, m_b, sigma_b)\n",
    "delta_Om = chi2_Om - marg_Om(Om, z_h, m_h, sigma_h)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Confidence interval limits\n",
    "q_lower = q0 - err_q0_menos\n",
    "q_upper = q0 + err_q0_mas\n",
    "\n",
    "Om_lower = Om - err_Om_menos\n",
    "Om_upper = Om + err_Om_mas\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 4.5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Left panel: q0\n",
    "ax1.plot(q_values, delta_q, lw=2.0)\n",
    "ax1.axhline(1, ls=\"--\", lw=1.5, color=\"gray\",\n",
    "            label=r\"$\\Delta \\chi^2 = 1$\")\n",
    "ax1.axvline(q0, ls=\":\", lw=1.8,\n",
    "            label=rf\"$q_0 = {q0:.3f}$\")\n",
    "ax1.axvspan(q_lower, q_upper, alpha=0.15)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel(r\"$q_0$\", fontsize=13)\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel(r\"$\\Delta \\chi^2_{\\mathrm{marg}}$\", fontsize=13)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1.set_xlim(q_values[0], q_values[-1])\n",
    "ax1.margins(x=0)\n",
    "ax1.set_ylim(0, delta_q.max()*1.02)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax1.tick_params(axis='both', labelsize=11)\n",
    "ax1.legend(loc=\"upper right\", fontsize=10, frameon=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Right panel: Om\n",
    "ax2.plot(Om_values, delta_Om, lw=2.0, color=\"C3\")\n",
    "ax2.axhline(1, ls=\"--\", lw=1.5, color=\"gray\",\n",
    "            label=r\"$\\Delta \\chi^2 = 1$\")\n",
    "ax2.axvline(Om, ls=\":\", lw=1.8, color=\"C3\",\n",
    "            label=rf\"$\\Omega_{{m,0}} = {Om:.3f}$\")\n",
    "ax2.axvspan(Om_lower, Om_upper, color=\"C3\", alpha=0.15)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax2.set_xlabel(r\"$\\Omega_{m,0}$\", fontsize=13)\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel(r\"$\\Delta \\chi^2_{\\mathrm{marg}}$\", fontsize=13)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax2.set_xlim(Om_values[0], Om_values[-1])\n",
    "ax2.margins(x=0)\n",
    "ax2.set_ylim(0, delta_Om.max()*1.02)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax2.tick_params(axis='both', labelsize=11)\n",
    "ax2.legend(loc=\"upper right\", fontsize=10, frameon=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(\"chi2_profiles_mnras.png\", dpi=300, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
